{{!-- partials/navigation.hbs — the primary/secondary nav items.

     RESERVED NAME: Ghost renders this from the `{{navigation}}` helper, never
     from `{{> navigation}}`. It emits only the <li> items — the parent <ul>
     decides the shape, which is what lets one partial serve three places:

       header   <ul class="ns-topnav__links">   a row
       footer   <ul>  inside .ns-footer__col    a column
       sheet    handled separately (see header.hbs) — the mobile sheet wants
                its own index numerals and chevrons, which would be noise in
                the other two.

     `aria-current="page"` rather than a class: .ns-topnav__link keys off the
     attribute a screen reader already announces, so the highlighted item and
     the announced item cannot drift apart. --}}
{{#foreach navigation}}
  <li>
    <a href="{{url absolute="true"}}" class="ns-topnav__link"{{#if current}} aria-current="page"{{/if}}>
      {{> "components/nav-icon" slug=slug}}<span>{{label}}</span>
    </a>
  </li>
{{/foreach}}
